course: dictionary
lesson: 8708
title: Who is the sender?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sender is the person who sends something. Send means to make something go from you to someone else, so the sender is the one who starts it on its way.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Return to sender» is written on a letter that could not be delivered, so it goes back to the person who sent it.
explain: «Do not open messages from unknown senders.» Unknown means you cannot tell who sent it, so the message could be unsafe. The words around sender tell you why it matters.
fact: A sender is the person who sends a letter, parcel, message or email.
fact: «Return to sender» means the letter goes back to the person who posted it.
fact: «Unknown sender» means you cannot tell who sent the message.
fact: Informal sports slang: a «send» or «sender» is a big, bold jump.
exercise: «Return to sender» is written on the envelope. Where should the letter go? | Into the bin straight away | *Back to the person who sent it | To the school office | On to the next house on the street
exercise: Mia gets an email from an unknown sender. What is the safest thing to do? | Forward it to all her friends | Open it and reply quickly | *Do not open it, and tell a trusted adult
exercise: Find and copy one word from «A broadcast, like radio or TV, goes from one sender to many listeners» that means the person who sends. | listeners | *sender | television | broadcast
test: In «A phone call goes from one person to another», who is the sender? | *The person who makes the call | The phone itself | The phone company | The person who answers the call
test: In «the sender paid a penny in advance», who paid? | The postman | The receiver | *The sender | The letter
exam: «You do not reply to mean messages; you save them, block the sender and report them.» What does sender mean here? | *The person who sent the mean message | The person who reads the message | The school | The phone company
